cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the descriptor data deposited with it, please cite
  the archived release below. Once the accompanying paper is published, cite that
  instead.
title: >-
  Activity cliffs on human acetylcholinesterase: a pre-registered escalation from
  2D descriptors to molecular dynamics
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for a ladder of five descriptor sets scored on
  activity cliffs of human acetylcholinesterase (CHEMBL220). The ladder runs from
  2D fingerprints through docked pose geometry, an eight-member receptor ensemble
  and MM/GBSA to descriptors extracted from 25 ns molecular dynamics trajectories,
  each scored on three framings of the endpoint against a matched ligand-based
  baseline on splits frozen before any descriptor was computed. The deposit
  carries the 229 per-run descriptor files, the curated ligand set, the frozen
  splits and every derived table, which together reproduce every number in the
  paper without rerunning a simulation. The reduced trajectories are available
  from the author on request.
